def pedal-power
  title "Pedal power entry: 9 V centre-negative jack, Schottky, 100 Ω / 100 µF, 4.5 V reference"
  about "A pedal's 9 V input: a 5.5 mm DC jack wired centre negative, an SS14 Schottky in the plus leg against a
      reversed plug, then 100 Ω and 100 µF as the filter of the audio rail, and the reference at half that rail – two
      10 kΩ with 100 µF. The parts are rated for a 12 or 18 V outlet as well (jack 24 V, diode 40 V, capacitors 35 V).
      Maker-coverage BL-17."
  port vplus "the protected supply behind the diode, unfiltered: relay coils, LEDs, a regulator for the logic"
  port out "the filtered rail for the audio stages (op-amp supplies)"
  port vref "half of out (4.5 V at 9 V): the bias of the audio stages"
  port gnd "ground"
  part J1 connector PJ-102AH lcsc C3096093 source reversible "{as}: 9 V DC jack, centre negative (pin 1 ground, pin 2
      plus)"
    nc barrel_switch
    notes "Centre negative: pin 1 (centre) ground, pin 2 (barrel) plus. Pin 3, the switch lug, is closed to pin 2
      without a plug – battery plus there, else in nc."
  part D1 diode SS14 lcsc C2480 "{as}: reverse-polarity Schottky in the plus leg"
  part R1 resistor 0805W8F1000T5E lcsc C17408 value 100 "{as}: supply filter 100 Ω"
  part C1 capacitor UWT1V101MCL1GS lcsc C125975 value 100uF "{as}: supply filter 100 µF 35 V"
  part R2 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: vref divider 10 k (top)"
  part R3 resistor 0805W8F1002T5E lcsc C17414 value 10k "{as}: vref divider 10 k (bottom)"
  part C2 capacitor UWT1V101MCL1GS lcsc C125975 value 100uF "{as}: vref 100 µF 35 V"
  net jack 0..18 V J1.barrel D1.anode
    notes "The jack's plus (barrel contact): a reversed plug reaches D1's anode only."
  net vplus 0..18 V D1.cathode R1.1
  net out 0..18 V R1.2 C1.plus R2.1
  net vref 0..9 V R2.2 R3.1 C2.plus
  net gnd J1.center C1.minus R3.2 C2.minus
  covers PATH.reverse LIM.v PATH.unfed HINT.pedal_supply HINT.jack_battery HINT.bulk
  notes "J1 centre negative, the pedal convention (HINT.pedal_supply): pin 1 (the 2.0 mm centre pin) ground, pin 2
      plus. J1 carries \"source\": \"reversible\": PATH.reverse checks that a centre-positive plug reaches only D1's
      anode. Check that the adapter's plug fits the 2.0 mm pin."
  notes "D1 SS14 in the plus leg – not in the ground leg, which the audio cables' shields bypass (HINT.pedal_supply):
      40 V reverse, so a reversed 18 V outlet stays within 0.67 × 40 V = 26.8 V; 1 A; VF ≤ 0.55 V at 1 A (MDD
      SS12…SS1200, Rev 2025A5). The library's AO3401A (block reverse-pmos) would drop less, but its gate allows ±12 V
      only – a 12 V outlet is at its limit, an 18 V one beyond."
  notes "R1 100 Ω and C1 100 µF: the audio rail's low-pass at 1/(2π · 100 Ω · 100 µF) = 15.9 Hz. R1 drops 0.1 V per mA
      (1 V at 10 mA, maker-coverage GTP 34) and carries 25 mA at most (0805, 1/8 W, 50 % derating): relay coils, LEDs
      and a logic regulator go on vplus, ahead of R1."
  notes "R2, R3 10 kΩ and C2 100 µF: vref at half of out with 5 kΩ source resistance – loads on vref at least 50 kΩ,
      10 × the divider (maker-coverage GTP 9); megohm bias resistors are far above. τ = 5 kΩ × 100 µF = 0.5 s: vref
      ramps up over about 2.5 s at power-on (the thump of GTP 9 is that ramp). C2 is the same part as C1 – more than
      the 10 µF the reference needs at least, one part fewer. The divider draws 0.45 mA at 9 V."
  notes "C1, C2 35 V: an 18 V outlet stays within 0.67 × 35 V = 23.5 V (maker-coverage GTP 36). The nets are declared
      up to 18 V (vref 9 V) – for 9 V supplies only, narrow them."
  notes "Battery: its plus on J1 pin 3 (remove it from nc), so the adapter's plug cuts it off; its minus through the
      input jack's ring contact (HINT.jack_battery)."
  notes "sim.json: J1 under sources (plus \"2\", minus \"1\") with the outlet's current limit as i_max_a, and its
      voltages under supplies (e.g. 8.5, 9, 9.6 V)."
  notes "A bulk capacitor on vplus as well where relay coils or LEDs switch there (HINT.bulk)."
  set test {
      "connect": {},
      "about": "vplus, out and vref become the nets T_VPLUS, T_OUT and T_VREF; the jack J1 becomes J2 – a 9 V source beside the example's 5 V J1",
      "sim": {
        "sources": {
          "J2": {
            "plus": "2",
            "minus": "1",
            "r_ohm": 0.5,
            "i_max_a": 0.1,
            "note": "values for the test: a 9 V outlet of a pedal supply, not a data sheet's"}},
        "supplies": {
          "usb-min": {"J1": 4.75, "J2": 8.5},
          "usb-nom": {"J1": 5.0, "J2": 9.0},
          "usb-max": {"J1": 5.25, "J2": 9.6}}}}
